    "# Quiz: Data Science in the Cloud: The \"Low code/No code\" way\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>One benefit of using Jupyter Notebooks is that you can quickly prototype models.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Jupyter Notebooks let you quickly prototype and test machine learning models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Jupyter Notebooks let you quickly prototype and test machine learning models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Why would a data scientist use Azure Machine Learning?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To save time exploring and pre-processing data.</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Saving time is one reason, but Azure ML also helps produce accurate models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To produce accurate models</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Accurate models are one reason, but Azure ML also saves time on data work.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Azure ML saves time by automating slow tasks, and it helps produce accurate models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>You don't need to have expertise in coding to use Azure ML.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The low code/no code way uses a graphical interface, with no prior knowledge of code required.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False, code is always needed</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The low code/no code way in Azure ML needs no prior knowledge of code.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What do you need to create before accessing Azure ML Studio?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>A workspace</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. You first create a workspace, then launch Azure ML Studio from it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>A compute instance</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Compute resources are created inside the workspace, so the workspace comes first.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>A compute cluster</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Compute resources are created inside the workspace, so the workspace comes first.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which of the following tasks are supported by Automated ML?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Image generation</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. AutoML tasks can be classification, regression or forecasting. Image generation is not one of them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Classification</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Classification is an AutoML task. In this project, you choose it to predict heart failure.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Natural language generation</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. AutoML tasks can be classification, regression or forecasting. Language generation is not one of them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-18-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>In which case do you need GPU over CPU?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When you have tabular data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Choose a GPU for the task it is best at: deep learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When you have enough money to afford it</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. GPUs do cost more, but you choose one because it is much better at deep learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>When you do Deep Learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. GPUs are built for parallel computing, so they are much better at deep learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
